        "faq-3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between Milk Tea Powder and Black Tea Granules?",
            "answer": "<p>Milk Tea Powder is a fine CTC dust, SRD grade, that brews fast and strong for milk tea. Black Tea Granules are CTC BOP (Broken Orange Pekoe), a granule grade and not a powder, for a brighter, cleaner cup.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-4": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does Cardamom Tea contain real cardamom?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We blend it ourselves: 60 g of cardamom from our own farm in Rajakumari for every 1 kg of tea from Vagamon. We choose a tea with medium flavour and strength so the cardamom comes through on top.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-5": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does the coffee contain chicory?",
            "answer": "<p>Our standard Naadan Kerala Coffee is a coffee and chicory blend, usually 53 parts coffee to 47 parts chicory. Chicory is a roasted root with no caffeine. It gives the decoction body and a darker colour. If you prefer a different mix, we also make 0% (no chicory), 10%, 20%, 30% and 43% chicory on request. Message us on WhatsApp at +91 88482 65849 and tell us the ratio you want.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-6": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How should I store tea and coffee?",
            "answer": "<p>Keep in an airtight container, away from direct sunlight and moisture.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-7": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much tea should I use for one cup?",
            "answer": "<p>We use 2 to 2.5 g of tea, about one level teaspoon, for a 180 ml cup of water and milk. Add a little more if you like it stronger.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-8": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What are the available pack sizes?",
            "answer": "<p>Milk Tea Powder: 250g, 500g, 1kg. Black Tea Granules: 200g, 400g, 800g. Cardamom Tea: 250g, 400g, 800g. Orange Pekoe: 50g, 100g, 200g. Filter Coffee: 250g, 400g.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-9": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When do I get free delivery?",
            "answer": "<p>Add any 2 items and delivery is free — two different teas or coffees, two sizes, or 2 packs of the same one. Orders above ₹649 also ship free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-10": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which is the best tea powder for kadak chai?",
            "answer": "<p>Premium Milk Tea Powder is selected specifically for strong, flavourful milk tea — it gives the colour, taste and aroma that makes a proper kadak chai. It works equally well for everyday chai patti.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-11": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is BOP tea? How is it different from dust tea?",
            "answer": "<p>BOP stands for Broken Orange Pekoe — a CTC broken-leaf grade that brews a brighter, cleaner cup than dust grades (like SRD). It gives more body and colour than dust with less bitterness. Our Premium Black Tea Granules are BOP grade, ideal for black tea and lighter milk tea.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq-12": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is the filter coffee chicory-free?",
            "answer": "<p>Our standard pack is not chicory-free: it is a coffee and chicory blend, usually 53 parts coffee to 47 parts chicory, the hotel-style mix many South Indian homes grew up with. But we do make chicory-free filter coffee (0% chicory), plus 10%, 20%, 30% and 43% chicory, and a Robusta and Arabica mix, on request. Message us on WhatsApp at +91 88482 65849. All of it is ground for South Indian filter preparation.</p>"
          }
        },
